$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh -d <T>_db src.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: cannot use PostgreSQL database <T>_db: connection to server <SERVER> failed: FATAL:  database "<T>_db" does not exist
[exit 1]

$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh -d <T>_empty src.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: PostgreSQL database <T>_empty has no yubikeys table; run 'yubikey-db.sh -b pg init-pg' first
[exit 1]

$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh -d <T>_db text.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: text.db is not a readable SQLite database
[exit 1]

$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh -d <T>_db other.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: other.db has no yubikeys table with the columns yubikey-db.sh uses
[exit 1]

$ PGHOST=127.0.0.1 PGUSER=<T>_radiator PGPASSWORD=test-only yubikey-db-migrate.sh -d <T>_db src.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: <T>_radiator cannot write to the yubikeys table in PostgreSQL database <T>_db or create temporary tables (is it a member of <T>_admin?)
[exit 1]

$ SQLITE3=<WORK>/sqlite3-tamper yubikey-db-migrate.sh -d <T>_db src.db
Source: src.db (snapshot taken <TIMESTAMP> UTC)
Target: PostgreSQL database <T>_db, mode new, AES keys stored as base64
Read 4 row(s) from the snapshot: 4 valid, 0 invalid
Inserted 4 row(s), with their counters
changed: 1 active value(s) like 'true' set to 1 (Radiator accepts only 1, so these keys could not log in before)
changed: 1 empty (NULL) active value(s) set to 1 (Radiator already treated them as active)
changed: 2 AES key(s) re-encoded as base64
changed: 1 private ID(s) converted from modhex to hex
changed: 1 invalid created time(s) replaced with the current time
MISMATCH: source row 3 (user olduser, public ID vvccccbbcdef): stored values differ from the source
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: verification failed; the changes were rolled back and PostgreSQL database <T>_db was not changed
[exit 1]

$ yubikey-db.sh -b pg -d <T>_db list
 username | public_id | active | created | accessed | counter 
----------+-----------+--------+---------+----------+---------
[exit 0]

